{% block user %}Selected the top {{ params.get('n_top_genes', 2000) }} highly variable genes (flavor={{ params.get('flavor', 'seurat') }}) to focus downstream dimensionality reduction on the genes carrying the most biological signal.{% endblock %}

{% block methods %}Highly variable genes were identified using sc.pp.highly_variable_genes from Scanpy with the '{{ params.get('flavor', 'seurat') }}' flavor, selecting the top {{ params.get('n_top_genes', 2000) }} genes by normalized dispersion{% if params.get('batch_key') %} computed per batch ({{ params.get('batch_key') }}) and combined across batches{% endif %}, following the feature-selection approach of Satija et al. [satija_hvg_2015]. Genes were flagged in adata.var['highly_variable'] without subsetting, so that subsequent principal component analysis could be restricted to these features while retaining the full gene set.{% endblock %}
